 5. ”Planning is the most critical phase of web development.” Discuss this statement by listing the key activities performed during the planning phase.
 ans:planning is considered as the most critical phase in the web development because it lays project's foundation , define goals etc. A well planned website reduces errors , saves time and ensure that the funal product meets the client's requirements.
 Key activities during the planning phase includes:
 i.Define goals and objectives:
 understanding the goals , objectives and features that the website should have.
 ii. Site map creation:
 Organizing the structure of the website and mapping how the pagges will connect.
 iii.Technology selection:
 deciding on which programming language , frameworks , databases and hosting options to choose.
 iv.Resource planning :
 Allocating team members ,tools, and buget for efficient.
 v.Timeline and milestones:
 setting deadlines for different stages of development to tarck progress.

 6. Explain the iterative nature of the Maintenance phase. Why is a website never truly
”finished”?
ans:The maintenance phase is called iterative which means it involves repeated updates and improvements rather than one time task. Websites are never truly "finished" because of the user needs , new technology and markets trends constantly change . During maintenance develpors fix bugs , update contents , add features , improve security and optimize performance . regular monitoring and iteration helps to ensure that the website will remain functional , relevant and user friendly over time.

